---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

export const prerender = true;

// Keep in sync with the canonical source in dvt/docs/08-legal/enterprise/terms-of-service.md
// (GTM-61) — edits must land in both repos.
const lastUpdated = 'July 30, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service — dvt"
  description="The terms governing self-serve, trial, and free use of dvt. Customers with a signed Cloud Service Agreement are governed by that agreement instead."
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          These Terms govern self-serve, trial, and free use of dvt. <strong>Customers with a
          signed Cloud Service Agreement are governed by that agreement, not these
          Terms.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="updated">Version 1.0 &middot; Effective {lastUpdated} &middot; Data Viz Tool, Inc.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container prose">
        <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are between you ("you") and <strong>Data Viz Tool, Inc.</strong>, a Utah
          corporation ("dvt", "we"). By creating an account or using the Service you agree to
          them. If you are agreeing on behalf of an organization, you represent that you have
          authority to bind it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Service</strong> means the dvt platform — the web application, REST API, and
          MCP interface.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>If you have a signed Cloud Service Agreement with us, that agreement governs
          and these Terms do not apply to your use under it.</strong>
        </p>

        <h2>2. Your account</h2>
        <p>
          You must provide accurate registration information and keep your credentials secure.
          You are responsible for all activity under your account and API keys, <strong>including
          actions taken by AI agents you authorize.</strong> Tell us promptly at
          <a href="mailto:security@dvt.dev">security@dvt.dev</a> if you suspect unauthorized
          access.
        </p>
        <p>You must be at least 16 years old.</p>

        <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          Your use is subject to the <a href="/aup">Acceptable Use Policy</a>, incorporated here.
          In particular, the
          Service is <strong>not authorized</strong> for protected health information, payment
          card data, or classified or export-controlled information.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Your data</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>You own your data.</strong> You retain all rights to your data, your dashboard
          specifications, and the content you create. You grant us only the license needed to
          operate the Service for you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>How the Service handles your data.</strong> dvt connects to data sources you
          control and executes queries <strong>on your infrastructure</strong>. Only result rows
          needed to render a visualization return to us, held in memory for that request and then
          discarded. <strong>We do not maintain a copy of your warehouse data.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          What we do store durably: your dashboard specifications, account metadata, audit
          records, envelope-encrypted connection credentials (ciphertext only), rendered exports,
          any files you upload, and — only if an administrator enables it — warehouse catalog
          metadata consisting of names, types, and comments, never data values.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>A specific caution:</strong> images and branding assets you upload are stored in
          a bucket readable by anyone holding the object's unguessable URL. <strong>Do not upload
          confidential material as dashboard media.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> describes our handling of personal data.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Trials and free access</h2>
        <p>
          We may offer trials and free access. These may be modified, limited, or discontinued at
          any time.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>When a trial ends, uploaded trial CSVs are deleted.</strong> Dashboard
          specifications, image exports, and account metadata are retained as described in our
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Export anything you want to keep before then —
          dashboard specifications export as JSON through the API.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Trials are provided "AS IS" with no warranty and no availability commitment of
          any kind.</strong>
        </p>

        <h2>6. Fees</h2>
        <p>
          Paid plans are billed as described at purchase. Fees are non-refundable except where
          these Terms or applicable law require otherwise. You are responsible for applicable
          taxes. We may change pricing on <strong>30 days' notice</strong>, effective at your next
          renewal.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Our intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          We own the Service, the software, and the dvt name and marks. These Terms grant you no
          rights in them beyond the right to use the Service.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Feedback.</strong> If you send us suggestions, you grant us a perpetual,
          royalty-free license to use them without obligation or attribution.
        </p>

        <h2>8. AI agents</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is designed to be operated by AI agents through its API and MCP interface.
          This is an intended use.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>You are responsible for what agents do under your credentials.</strong> Agent
          actions are recorded and attributed in the audit log, but attribution is not
          authorization — an API key acts with whatever authority you gave it. Scope keys
          narrowly.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>If you connect a third-party AI tool to dvt, the data that tool receives leaves
          our control</strong> and is governed by that tool's terms, not ours.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>You may stop using the Service and delete your account at any time.</p>
        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate your access if you materially breach these Terms or the
          <a href="/aup">Acceptable Use Policy</a>, or if required by law. <strong>Except where a
          violation poses an
          immediate threat to the security or availability of the Service or to another customer's
          data, we will contact you first and give you a reasonable opportunity to
          remedy.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          On termination, you may export your data for <strong>30 days</strong>. After that, we
          delete or de-identify your data on the schedule described in our
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> — note that image exports are retained indefinitely
          unless you ask us to remove them.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY
          KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE,
          AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or secure, or that
          results obtained through it will be accurate.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>No availability commitment applies to use under these Terms.</strong> Service
          level commitments are available only under a signed Cloud Service Agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>dvt is a visualization tool. It renders what your queries return. You are
          responsible for the correctness of your queries, your data, and any decisions you make
          from them.</strong>
        </p>

        <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, NEITHER PARTY IS LIABLE FOR INDIRECT,
          INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR LOST PROFITS, REVENUE, OR
          DATA.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>OUR TOTAL LIABILITY ARISING FROM OR RELATING TO THESE TERMS WILL NOT EXCEED THE
          GREATER OF (A) THE FEES YOU PAID US IN THE TWELVE MONTHS PRECEDING THE EVENT, OR (B) US
          $100.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          These limits do not apply to liability that cannot be limited by law, or to either
          party's gross negligence or willful misconduct.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Indemnity</h2>
        <p>
          You will defend and indemnify us against third-party claims arising from your data,
          your use of the Service in breach of these Terms or the
          <a href="/aup">Acceptable Use Policy</a>, or your
          violation of law or third-party rights.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms. <strong>Material changes take effect 30 days after we post
          them or notify you</strong>, whichever is later. Continued use after the effective date
          constitutes acceptance. If you do not agree, stop using the Service and delete your
          account before the effective date.
        </p>

        <h2>14. General</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Governing law:</strong> Utah, excluding conflict-of-laws rules.
          <strong>Venue:</strong> state and federal courts in Salt Lake County, Utah.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Assignment:</strong> you may not assign these Terms without our consent; we may
          assign to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all assets.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Entire agreement:</strong> these Terms, the
          <a href="/aup">Acceptable Use Policy</a>, and the Privacy Policy are the entire
          agreement for use not covered by a signed Cloud Service Agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Severability:</strong> if a provision is unenforceable, the rest remains in
          effect.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:legal@dvt.dev">legal@dvt.dev</a> &middot; Data
          Viz Tool, Inc., 7533 S Center View Ct, Ste N, West Jordan, UT 84084.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--space-16) 0 var(--space-12);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-neutral-200);
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-brand-mark);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .page-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-3xl), 5vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-neutral-600);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 680px;
  }
  .updated {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-neutral-500);
  }

  .section { padding: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-16); }

  .prose { max-width: 720px; }
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    margin: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-4);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .prose p {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .prose strong { color: var(--color-neutral-900); font-weight: 600; }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-brand-mark);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .prose a:hover { color: var(--color-neutral-900); }
</style>
